From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] input: edt-ft5x06: keep the IRQ enabled when resume re-init fails

edt_ft5x06_ts_resume() disables the controller IRQ before re-running the
probe-time initialization, but the re-identify failure path returns
immediately:

	ret = edt_ft5x06_ts_identify(client, tsdata);
	if (ret) {
		dev_err(dev, "touchscreen re-identify failed\n");
		return ret;
	}

The IRQ was disabled just above on retain-power boards (0019) and in the
suspend path on every other board, so that return skips enable_irq() and
leaves it disabled: the touchscreen stays dead until
51-thorch-touchscreen-reprobe unbinds/rebinds the controller or the device
reboots. Route the failure through a label that enables the IRQ first.

Fixes: 0019-input-edt-ft5x06-reinit-on-resume.patch
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ static int edt_ft5x06_ts_resume(struct device *dev)
 		ret = edt_ft5x06_ts_identify(client, tsdata);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "touchscreen re-identify failed\n");
-			return ret;
+			goto out_enable_irq;
 		}
 
 		/*
@@ -91,6 +91,15 @@ static int edt_ft5x06_ts_resume(struct device *dev)
 		edt_ft5x06_ts_get_defaults(&client->dev, tsdata);
 		edt_ft5x06_ts_get_parameters(tsdata);
 		edt_ft5x06_restore_reg_parameters(tsdata);
+
+out_enable_irq:
+		/*
+		 * A failed re-identify lands here instead of returning
+		 * straight away: the IRQ was disabled above on retain-power
+		 * boards and in the suspend path on every other board, so
+		 * skipping enable_irq() leaves the controller dead until a
+		 * re-probe or a reboot.
+		 */
 		enable_irq(tsdata->client->irq);
 	}
 
